  "id": "ableism",
  "term": "ableism",
  "definition": "Ableism is a pattern of beliefs and actions that devalue, exclude, or mistreat people with disabilities by judging them against able-bodied norms. It can show up as stereotyping, prejudice, discrimination, social exclusion, oppression, or abusive and exploitative behavior at individual, organizational, or societal levels.",
